{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Mechanism (confirmed via 4-phase debug, 2026-09-10): ChatGPT.app codex (single long-lived process, PID 11153 this boot) launches a fresh MCP server stack (uvx serena start-mcp-server --context codex + pyright-langserver + node + headroom mcp wrapper) per conversation epoch and leaves prior stacks running when conversations end. Because codex itself stays alive, the stale stacks keep a live parent (never PPID 1) and so evade the mem-sentinel PPID-1 orphan sweeper shipped for centauric-gnomic-hake — this is the surviving variant of that defect class. Stale stacks (~1.2GB each; 4 epochs Sep 6/7/9/10 observed) go fully swapped-out and stop draining FSEventStreams while remaining registered clients; under rebar's fs-event volume fseventsd accretes buffers without bound and never returns memory (peak==current): 107GB phys_footprint by day 4 of the Sep 6 boot (27.2GB RSS + 79.8GB swapped, 136.8M live mallocs, 47.8M path strings), swap 67/68.6GB — near-recurrence of incident 2ab6-bae5-8ca4-429c. Claude/Copilot ide-assistant serena instances do not accumulate. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (all delivered 2026-09-10): AC1 sanctioned config decided+documented — serena DISABLED for codex (~/.codex/config.toml enabled=false with incident annotation; re-enable only with a reaping/idle-exit mechanism; takes effect at app restart since codex respawns from launch-time config, observed respawn 09:57:12). AC2 monitoring — mem-sentinel already snapshots fseventsdKB every 5 min and reaps PPID-1 serena orphans; the codex-alive-parent evasion gap is mooted by AC1 (no new mechanism added). AC3 remediation verified live — stale stacks killed by pid; operator restarted fseventsd via sudo kill (SIP blocks launchctl kickstart): fseventsd 107GB -> 10.9MB, swap used 67GB -> 18.4GB, free RAM ~0.1GB -> ~52GB, no reboot. Ongoing observation is operational via ~/Library/Logs/mem-sentinel.log, deliberately not a ticket-held wait. Validation: live host measurements in comments; evidence in .rebar/scratch/memleak-copilot-87759/ and comments on 2ab6-bae5-8ca4-429c."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789059806653790001,"uuid":"2fd92410-ddd8-4e9e-835e-46f8856b09cb"}